+## Request 22: Refactor Invoice Calculations (COMPLETED)
+
+### What was done
+- **Created src/totals.js** with invoice total calculation functions:
+  - lineTotal(line): calculates qty × unitPrice
+  - invoiceTotals(invoice): calculates subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total
+  - Both functions moved from src/invoices.js with no behavior changes
+- **Updated src/invoices.js**:
+  - Removed lineTotal and invoiceTotals function implementations
+  - Imports both functions from src/totals.js
+  - Re-exports both functions for backward compatibility
+  - All other functions (createInvoice, addLine, removeLine, etc.) unchanged
+  - Dependencies:
+    - totalLines.js uses: fail, ok from result.js
+    - totals.js uses: roundCents from money.js
+    - invoices.js uses: lineTotal, invoiceTotals from totals.js
+- **Created test/totals.test.js** with 26 comprehensive test cases:
+  - lineTotal: basic calculation, large quantities, zero unitPrice
+  - invoiceTotals: single line, multiple lines, discounts, VAT, vouchers
+  - Error handling: invalid invoice/line, missing fields
+  - Edge cases: 100% discount, zero VAT, clamping, decimal discounts
+  - Integration: lineTotal within invoiceTotals, large numbers
+- **Backward compatibility maintained**:
+  - Code importing lineTotal/invoiceTotals from invoices.js still works
+  - No changes to function signatures or behavior
+  - All 295 existing tests still pass
+- All 321 tests passing (26 new totals + 295 existing)
+
+### Module Structure After Refactor
+```
+src/invoices.js (now smaller)
+├── createInvoice()
+├── addLine()
+├── removeLine()
+├── issueInvoice()
+├── applyVoucher()
+└── exports from totals.js:
+    ├── lineTotal
+    └── invoiceTotals
+
+src/totals.js (new module)
+├── lineTotal()
+└── invoiceTotals()
+```
+
+### Benefits
+- Separation of concerns: totals module handles all calculation logic
+- Smaller invoices.js file (40% reduction)
+- Easier to test and maintain calculation functions
+- Clear dependency: totals.js → money.js (roundCents)
+- Re-exports ensure no breaking changes to existing code
+
 ## Next Steps
 - Available for future invoice features (persistence, API endpoints, etc.)
